  "description": "Finest is another decades-old, honored Fuji model name.\n\nLike the Roubaix and Roubaix Pro, Finest frames are made from two materials,\n\naluminum and steel. The Finest is the butted Cro-Moly steel version.\n\nThe Finest frame has rear eyelets for mounting a luggage rack or pannier mounts.\n\nIf you're struggling to decide between Finest and Finest-AL, and you plan\n\nto do some loaded touring, those eyelets may just sway you toward the Finest.\n\nFinest forks are butted, tapered, aero-shaped Cro-Moly steel. Nice forks.\n\nThe equipment is all competent, dependable stuff, mostly Shimano Sora. Three chainrings, lots of gears, not much weight, tons\n\nof versatility. Dual-Pivot brakes; 32 sturdy stainless steel spokes per wheel;\n\nsealed, low-maintenance bottom bracket. A Finest would be perfect for weekend\n\nclub not-so-social outings. Those rides would be fine preparation for three\n\nweeks wandering Ireland in the autumn. A Finest would be happy pushing the\n\npace on club rides, yet stable and supple in its ride: A joyous companion\n\non ancient Irish lanes or your favorite bike path.",
